            <ArticleTitle>Sclerosing Angiomatoid Nodular Transformation of Spleen in a 3-year-old Child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1081-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Reports of sclerosing angiomatoid nodular transformation in the pediatric population are rare.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE CHARACTERISTICS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The 3-year-old child was injured in a car accident and then diagnosed with sclerosing angiomatoid nodular transformation. The patient underwent exploratory surgery with partial splenectomy including total excision of the tumor mass.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Neither recurrence nor metastasis occurred over 20 months of follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MESSAGE" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Sclerosing angiomatoid nodular transformation can occur in early childhood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
